# Web + iOS + Android auth parity

When the user asks for an auth or account-security change on **any** of the web app (`docs/`), the iOS app (`on-call wizard/`), or the Android app (`android/`), apply the **same behavior on all three** unless they explicitly say “web only”, “iOS only”, or “Android only”.

## Covered surfaces

- Sign in / sign up (email + password)
- Email verification (6-digit OTP, not magic links)
- Google and Apple OAuth
- Authenticator MFA / 2FA (TOTP)
- Session handling, sign-out, password reset (when implemented)
- Role selection for new OAuth users (Doctor / Hospital)

## How to implement

1. Update web: `docs/assets/js/store.js`, `docs/assets/js/domain/mfa.js`, `docs/assets/js/views/auth.js`, `docs/assets/js/app.js`, and related CSS.
2. Update iOS: `on-call wizard/Supabase/SupabaseAuthService.swift`, `on-call wizard/AuthView.swift`, and any credentials/security UI.
3. Update Android: `android/app/src/main/java/com/eporthospine/mdshift/data/AuthCoordinator.kt`, `android/app/src/main/java/com/eporthospine/mdshift/ui/AuthScreens.kt`, and the credential / Custom Tabs wiring in `MainActivity.kt`.
4. Keep copy, error messages, and flow order aligned (e.g. signup → email OTP → optional MFA enroll → app).
5. Document dashboard steps once in `supabase/AUTH_SETUP.md` (applies to every client). Android redirect and Play setup details also live in `android/README.md`.

## Do not

- Ship OAuth or MFA on only one platform by default
- Use magic-link confirm emails when the product standard is 6-digit codes
